* Fri Aug 21 2026 Nicolas Souveton <souvetonnicolas@gmail.com> 0.8.5-1
- Share photos from the photo viewer, a person, a day, a trip or a memory
- Sharing now goes through the standard Sailfish share sheet, so it actually
  reaches Bluetooth, e-mail and your accounts
- A person's photos are sorted by date, newest first, with a switch to oldest
  first; they used to come out in the order they happened to be scanned
- Show only the matches still waiting for confirmation, so reviewing them is
  no longer all or nothing
- Double tap in the photo viewer zooms in where you tapped, instead of only
  resetting the zoom
- The zoom buttons keep the middle of the screen in view rather than jumping
  to the top-left corner
- Zooming and panning no longer drift into the empty space beside a photo,
  and a rotated photo is refitted to the screen
- The photo viewer now shows the photo's details and its location map right
  under the image, with no menu to open first
- Copy a photo's file path from the details, and share it from there too
- Pick which photos to share: a selection mode on people, days, trips and
  memories, with a warning once the selection is too heavy to go through
- Confirm a single suggested match from a person's photo grid, rather than
  having to accept every match at once
- Filter and sort a person's photos from the page itself instead of the
  pulley menu
- Fix the long-press menu being drawn over the neighbouring photos
- Fix the last column of a photo grid being cut off by the edge of the
  screen, and give the grid room to breathe
- Take back a confirmation on a single photo, which also makes "Confirm all
  matches" undoable
- Fix English counts reading "1 people" and "1 photos"
- Translations completed for French, Italian, Spanish, Finnish, German and
  Norwegian

* Tue Aug 18 2026 Nicolas Souveton <souvetonnicolas@gmail.com> 0.8.4-1
- Fix a crash when identifying a face, whether by typing a new name or by
  picking a contact from the address book
- Fix the trip route map drawing as an empty sheet of paper
- Trip map now fills in land and sea instead of sketching a bare coastline
- Trip map keeps true proportions, with a scale bar valid in every direction
- Trip stops are grouped by place at the scale of the trip, and the map marks
  the places you spent time in rather than every photo taken along the way
- Slightly rounder Trip and Hidden badges in the Events list
- Fix a crash when merging two people, same cause as the one above
- The app no longer writes its private file paths to the system journal on
  every launch, and reports a diagnosable backtrace if it ever does crash

* Tue Aug 18 2026 Nicolas Souveton <souvetonnicolas@gmail.com> 0.8.3-1
- Suggest who a face belongs to while identifying, confirmed with a single tap
- Fix tapping a name in the identification autocomplete not selecting it
- People created during a review are now suggested for the next faces
- Backups no longer carry contact links, which point to contacts of the old device

* Sun Aug 02 2026 Nicolas Souveton <souvetonnicolas@gmail.com> 0.8.2-1
- Group several days into a named trip; auto-suggest trips based on distance from home
- Trip detail page: browse by day or by geographic stop, route distance, offline route map with a bundled world coastline sketch
- Add more days, merge, ungroup, or hide a day/trip from the Events list; custom cover photo per day or trip
- Optional setting to include photos without an identified person in Events
- Animated polaroid-style cover page
- Fix cover page rendering blank on device
- Fix trip map/distance being thrown off by a single photo with a corrupted GPS coordinate
- Fix "Ungroup" doing nothing

* Sat Aug 01 2026 Nicolas Souveton <souvetonnicolas@gmail.com> 0.8.1-1
- Add a Language setting to override the app language independently of the system locale
- Enable the Norwegian Bokmål (nb_NO) translation added in the previous release

* Mon Jul 13 2026 Nicolas Souveton <souvetonnicolas@gmail.com> 0.8.0-1
- About page: app logo, dynamic version, updated feature list
- Version bump consolidating all 0.7.x changes since the 0.7.1 release

